{"id":45731,"name":"Washington County","slug":"washington-county","state":"Wisconsin","code":"WI","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/wisconsin-property-investments-the-benefits-of-tax-deed-sales/washington-county/","lastUpdated":"2026-07-20T14:57:20","facts":null,"bodyHtml":"<div class=\"yoast-breadcrumbs\"><span><span><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/\">Home</a></span> » <span><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/\">Tax Deed</a></span> » <span><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/\">Tax Deed States</a></span> » <span><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/wisconsin-property-investments-the-benefits-of-tax-deed-sales/\">Wisconsin Tax Deed Investments: The Benefits of Tax Deed Sales</a></span> » <span class=\"breadcrumb_last\" aria-current=\"page\">Washington County</span></span></div>\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<span class=\"uZY8wiDmPfXSRtqdBNCJK25HQxhvW34npolGsLac7AF6zOMrU1gEVb\"><iframe title=\"Beginner Tax Deed Investing (Step By Step)\" width=\"1170\" height=\"658\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/5RJylhmyFtI?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></span>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-yoast-seo-estimated-reading-time yoast-reading-time__wrapper\"><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" data-icon=\"clock\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.1em\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" d=\"M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__spacer\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:1em\"></span><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__descriptive-text\">Estimated reading time: </span><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__reading-time\">5</span><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__time-unit\"> minutes</span></p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Author:</strong>&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://taxlienschool.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">TLS Team</mark></a></strong><br><strong>Reviewed by:</strong>&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://taxlienschool.com/josh-blanchard-tax-lien-school/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Josh Blanchard</mark></a></strong><br><strong>Fact Checked by:</strong>&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://taxlienschool.com/jack-aldous-tax-lien-school/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Jack Aldous</mark></a></strong></p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<p>Washington, Wisconsin, tax deeds allow regular people to buy land and buildings that the county took because owners did not pay property taxes. If you want to learn more about Washington, Wisconsin Tax Deeds, this guide explains how the process works, where to find current listings, and what steps to take before you bid.</p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-yoast-seo-table-of-contents yoast-table-of-contents\"><h3>Table of contents</h3><ul><li><a href=\"#h-what-is-a-tax-deed\" data-level=\"2\">What Is a Tax Deed?</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-who-runs-the-sale-in-washington-county-wisconsin\" data-level=\"2\">Who Runs the Sale in Washington County, Wisconsin?</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-how-washington-county-wisconsin-tax-deed-sales-work\" data-level=\"2\">How Washington County Wisconsin Tax Deed Sales Work</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-how-to-bid-on-a-washington-wisconsin-tax-deed-property\" data-level=\"2\">How to Bid on a Washington, Wisconsin Tax Deed Property</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-why-buyers-should-be-careful-when-buying-washington-wisconsin-tax-deeds\" data-level=\"2\">Why Buyers Should Be Careful When Buying Washington Wisconsin Tax Deeds?</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-quick-facts-table\" data-level=\"2\">Quick Facts Table</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-frequently-asked-questions\" data-level=\"2\">Frequently Asked Questions</a></li></ul></div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-what-is-a-tax-deed\"><strong>What Is a Tax Deed?</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>When a property owner does not pay real estate taxes, the debt becomes delinquent. If the taxes stay unpaid long enough, the county can take legal title to the property. This is called a tax deed. The county then sells these properties to the public to recover the unpaid taxes.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n\n\n<p>This is different from a &#8220;tax lien.&#8221; Wisconsin does not sell tax lien certificates like some other states. Instead, the county eventually takes full ownership and then sells the property outright. That is why the process is called Washington County tax deeds, not tax liens.</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-yoast-seo-ai-summarize yoast-ai-summarize\"><h3>Key Takeaways</h3>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list yoast-ai-summarize-list\">\n<li>Washington, Wisconsin Tax Deeds allow the purchase of properties taken by the county for unpaid taxes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The Washington County Treasurer&#8217;s Office handles tax deed sales, partnering with Wisconsin Surplus for online auctions.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Bidders must create an account, read property listings, and do their own research before participating in the auction.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Properties are sold &#8216;as is&#8217;, so buyers should verify property conditions, liens, and zoning restrictions.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Key auction details include a 1.5% monthly interest on unpaid taxes and a requirement for payment within set auction terms.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-who-runs-the-sale-in-washington-county-wisconsin\"><strong>Who Runs the Sale in Washington County, Wisconsin?</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The <strong>Washington County Treasurer&#8217;s Office</strong> manages delinquent tax collection and the resulting property sales. The county partners with <strong>Wisconsin Surplus</strong>, an outside auction company based in Mount Horeb, to run the actual online bidding for tax deed properties. Wisconsin Surplus has handled state and county government auctions since 2003.</p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-how-washington-county-wisconsin-tax-deed-sales-work\"><strong>How Washington County Wisconsin Tax Deed Sales Work</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The process moves through a few clear stages before a property lands on the auction site.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Stage</strong></td><td><strong>What Happens</strong></td></tr><tr><td>1. Taxes go unpaid</td><td>Real estate taxes become delinquent starting February 1, with 1.5% monthly interest and penalty added</td></tr><tr><td>2. Delinquency grows</td><td>Taxes stay unpaid for multiple years without the owner redeeming (paying back) the debt</td></tr><tr><td>3. County takes title</td><td>Washington County obtains a tax deed and becomes the legal owner</td></tr><tr><td>4. Property is listed</td><td>The parcel is posted on the Wisconsin Surplus auction site for public bidding</td></tr><tr><td>5. Auction closes</td><td>The highest qualifying bidder wins; funds go toward recovering unpaid taxes</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-how-to-bid-on-a-washington-wisconsin-tax-deed-property\"><strong>How to Bid on a Washington, Wisconsin Tax Deed Property</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"schema-how-to wp-block-yoast-how-to-block\"><p class=\"schema-how-to-description\">Follow these steps if you want to bid on a tax deed property in Washington County.</p> <ol class=\"schema-how-to-steps\"><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1784574192872\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Create a free account</strong> on the Wisconsin Surplus bidding site.</strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\"></p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1784574225327\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Search current auctions</strong> and filter by Washington County to see available parcels.</strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\"></p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1784574231995\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Read the listing carefully.</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">Check the parcel number, legal description, photos, and any notes about condition or access.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1784574248513\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Do your own research.</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">Look up the parcel on the county&#8217;s Tax Inquiry tool and Register of Deeds records before bidding. Properties are sold &#8220;as is.&#8221;</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1784574267435\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Register to bid</strong> and place your maximum bid or watch the live auction countdown.</strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\"></p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1784574276828\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Pay promptly if you win.</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">Wisconsin Surplus requires payment and closing steps within the timeframe stated in the auction terms.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1784574284800\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Record the deed.</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">Once payment clears, the county issues you a deed, which you then record with the Register of Deeds.</p> </li></ol></div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Washington-County-Wisconsin-1.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Washington-County-Wisconsin-1-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Washington-County-Wisconsin-1-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Washington-County-Wisconsin-1-768x512.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Washington-County-Wisconsin-1.webp\" height=\"720\" width=\"1081\" srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Washington-County-Wisconsin-1.webp 1081w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Washington-County-Wisconsin-1-541x360.webp 541w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Washington-County-Wisconsin-1-296x197.webp 296w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Washington-County-Wisconsin-1-768x512.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" class=\"wp-image-45732 sp-no-webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"  > </picture></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Book a Call with Dustin Hahn</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-why-buyers-should-be-careful-when-buying-washington-wisconsin-tax-deeds\"><strong>Why Buyers Should Be Careful When Buying Washington Wisconsin Tax Deeds?</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Tax deed properties are sold &#8220;as is,&#8221; with no guarantee about the condition of the building or land. Some parcels may have back liens, code violations, or access problems. Before bidding, it helps to:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Check the property on the county&#8217;s online <strong>Tax Inquiry</strong> tool for ownership and parcel history.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Look at the <strong>Register of Deeds</strong> land records for prior liens or issues.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drive by or view the property in person if possible.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Confirm zoning and use restrictions with the local municipality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-quick-facts-table\"><strong>Quick Facts </strong>Table </h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Item</strong></td><td><strong>Detail</strong></td></tr><tr><td>County agency</td><td>Washington County Treasurer</td></tr><tr><td>Auction partner</td><td>Wisconsin Surplus (Mount Horeb, WI)</td></tr><tr><td>Governing law</td><td>Wisconsin Statutes, Chapters 74 and 75</td></tr><tr><td>Sale type</td><td>Tax deed (full ownership transfer), not a lien certificate</td></tr><tr><td>Delinquency start</td><td>February 1 each year</td></tr><tr><td>Interest/penalty</td><td>1.5% per month on unpaid taxes</td></tr><tr><td>Property condition</td><td>Sold &#8220;as is,&#8221; buyer does own research</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-frequently-asked-questions\"><strong>Frequently Asked Questions</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"schema-faq wp-block-yoast-faq-block\"><div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784574313843\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>What are Washington Wisconsin tax deeds?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">They are properties that Washington County, Wisconsin took ownership of after owners failed to pay real estate taxes. The county then sells these properties to the public through auction.</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784574338667\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Where can I find current tax deed listings for Washington County?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Listings appear on the Wisconsin Surplus auction website, which is linked from the Washington County Treasurer&#8217;s page under &#8220;Wisconsin Surplus (Tax Deed Properties).&#8221;</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784574355091\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Does Washington County sell tax lien certificates?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">No. Wisconsin counties, including Washington County, sell tax deeds after taking full title to a property, not lien certificates.</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784574366345\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Is there a minimum bid?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Wisconsin law generally requires the county to reject bids below the appraised value. Each listing on Wisconsin Surplus shows the specific terms for that property.</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784574378559\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Can I inspect a tax deed property before bidding?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">You can view listing photos and descriptions online. Some properties may allow drive-by viewing, but interior access is usually not guaranteed since properties are sold &#8220;as is.&#8221;</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784574391425\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>How do I check if a property has other debts or liens?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Use the Washington County Tax Inquiry tool and search Register of Deeds land records before you bid.</p> </div> </div>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-yoast-seo-related-links yoast-seo-related-links\">\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/wisconsin-property-investments-the-benefits-of-tax-deed-sales/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Wisconsin Tax Deed Investments: The Benefits of Tax Deed Sales</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/wisconsin-property-investments-the-benefits-of-tax-deed-sales/brown-county/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Brown County</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/wisconsin-property-investments-the-benefits-of-tax-deed-sales/winnebago-county/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Winnebago County</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/wisconsin-property-investments-the-benefits-of-tax-deed-sales/rock-county/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Rock County</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/auction-calendar-event/washington-county-florida-tax-deed-auction-2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Washington County FL – Tax Deed Auction</mark></a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>Sign up or log in to view the full content.</em></p><div id=\"popup-overlay\"></div><div id=\"signup-popup\" style=\"text-align: center; padding: 20px;\"><h4>Get Instant Free Access To The Training Vault Now</h4><p>Learn how to get 18-36% returns on your investment and buy property for as little as $500 with tax lien and tax deeds.</p><div class=\"video-container\" style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin: 20px 0;\"><iframe src=\"https://youtube.com/embed/FkB-M8RaSHo\" allowfullscreen style=\"width: 100%; max-width: 560px; height: 315px; border: none; border-radius: 8px;\"></iframe></div><div class=\"button-container\" style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 10px;\"><button style=\"padding: 10px 20px; font-size: 16px; cursor: pointer;\">Sign Up for FREE Access</button><button style=\"padding: 10px 20px; font-size: 16px; cursor: pointer;\">Already a Member? Login</button></div></div>","upcomingCount":0}